{"Title":"Special Election for the Worcester and Hampshire district","BillNumber":"S2404","DocketNumber":"SD2657","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"KES0","Name":"Karen E. Spilka","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KES0","ResponseDate":"2023-06-13T11:45:13.613"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"KES0","Name":"Karen E. Spilka","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KES0","ResponseDate":"2023-06-14T12:12:32.99"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2404/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, June 15, 2023 -- Offered by Senator Spilka relative to setting the date for a special election to fill the vacancy in the Worcester and Hampshire senatorial district.","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That by the authority of article IV of section II of chapter I of the Constitution, the Senate declares that, by reason of the resignation of Anne M. Gobi as senator from the Worcester and Hampshire district, the office of senator from the Worcester and Hampshire district is vacant. By the authority of article XXIV of the Amendments to the Constitution, the Senate directs the president of the Senate to issue a precept setting forth November 7, 2023, as the day for holding an election to fill the vacancy in the Worcester and Hampshire district, city of Gardner, the city of Worcester, Ward 7 Precincts 2, 4, 5, 6, Ward 9 Precincts 3, and 4, and the towns of Barre, Brookfield, East Brookfield, Hardwick, Holden, Hubbardston, Leicester, New Braintree, North Brookfield, Oakham, Paxton, Phillipston, Princeton, Rutland, Spencer, Sterling, Templeton, West Brookfield and Westminster in the county of Worcester; and the town of Ware in the county of Hampshire.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}